  "interpretation": [
    "AC completed all four fixed AccessCheck controls with [3,0,1,2] and qualified.",
    "The arm requested with AAP policy 1 completed only the combined control: API true, AccessStatus true, mask 3 and zero privileges; its fixed expectation was mask 2. This is a real semantic-mask mismatch, not a failed AccessCheck API or an initialized output.",
    "The combined descriptor has the same byte hash in both arms and its metadata matches the fixed source template. No descriptor bytes or SIDs are included here.",
    "The source stops the observer immediately on the mask mismatch, so world/AAP/ARAP controls were not run for the second arm. No complete LPAC vector or AC classification is inferred from that single call.",
    "The second proof generation_after is false because the observer exited before that final check. This flag is not a recorded generation mismatch; separately, the owner performed valid held checks after the observer returned.",
    "AccessCheck API success and AccessStatus false are distinct. The AC world control is a successful negative; its Win32 error is null because the wrapper does not interpret LastError on API success.",
    "The arm policy argument and successful construction do not prove LPAC semantics. Which layer accepted, modified, ignored or overrode the attribute remains unknown.",
    "Both transfers and later exact Job/primary identity admissions succeeded, but this finite no-resume cell does not prove atomic inner creation, continuous outer supervision from creation or resolution of a crash transfer gap.",
    "Worker exit 0 means the owner emitted its failed-accesscheck report; both never-resumed actors were stopped with observed exit 1. No successful identity mechanism, DNS/proxy isolation or product acceptance is inferred.",
    "Known caller cleanup closed this new environment obligation. It does not prove external environment absence or broker cancellation, and original atomic01 unknown/recovery remains unchanged."
